ns.html#module-PIL.SunImagePlugin","signature":null},{"path":"PIL.TarIO","kind":"package","dispname":"TarIO","docUri":"https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/PIL.html#module-PIL.TarIO","signature":null},{"path":"PIL.TgaImagePlugin","kind":"package","dispname":"TgaImagePlugin","docUri":"https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/plugins.html#module-PIL.TgaImagePlugin","signature":null},{"path":"PIL.TiffImagePlugin","kind":"package","dispname":"TiffImagePlugin","docUri":"https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/plugins.html#module-PIL.TiffImagePlugin","signature":null},{"path":"PIL.TiffTags","kind":"module","dispname":"TiffTags","docUri":"https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/TiffTags.html#module-PIL.TiffTags","signature":null},{"path":"PIL.UnidentifiedImageError","kind":"class","dispname":"UnidentifiedImageError","docUri":"https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/PIL.html#PIL.UnidentifiedImageError","signature":"(...)","doc":"Raised in :py:meth:`PIL.Image.open` if an image cannot be opened and identified.\n\nIf a PNG image raises this error, setting :data:`.ImageFile.LOAD_TRUNCATED_IMAGES`\nto true may allow the image to be opened after all. The setting will ignore missing\ndata and checksum failures.","doc_summary":"Raised in :py:meth:`PIL.Image.open` if an image cannot be opened and identified."},{"path":"PIL.WalImageFile","kind":"package","dispname":"WalImageFile","docUri":"https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/PIL.html#module-PIL.WalImageFile","signature":null,"doc":"This reader is based on the specification available from:\nhttps://www.flipcode.com/archives/Quake_2_BSP_File_Format.shtml\nand has been tested with a few sample files found using google.\n\n.. note::\n    This format cannot be automatically recognized, so the reader\n    is not registered for use with :py:func:`PIL.Image.open()`.\n    To open a WAL file, use the :py:func:`PIL.WalImageFile.open()` function instead.","doc_summary":"This reader is based on the specification available from: https://www.flipcode.com/archives/Quake_2_BSP_File_Format.shtml and has been tested with a few sample files found using google."},{"path":"PIL.WebPImagePlugin","kind":"package","dispname":"WebPImagePlugin","docUri":"https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/plugins.html#module-PIL.WebPImagePlugin","signature":null},{"path":"PIL.WmfImagePlugin","kind":"package","dispname":"WmfImagePlugin","docUri":"https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/plugins.html#module-PIL.WmfImagePlugin","signature":null},{"path":"PIL.XVThumbImagePlugin","kind":"package","dispname":"XVThumbImagePlugin","docUri":"https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/plugins.html#module-PIL.XVThumbImagePlugin","signature":null},{"path":"PIL.XbmImagePlugin","kind":"package","dispname":"XbmImagePlugin","docUri":"https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/plugins.html#module-PIL.XbmImagePlugin","signature":null},{"path":"PIL.XpmImagePlugin","kind":"package","dispname":"XpmImagePlugin","docUri":"https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/plugins.html#module-PIL.XpmImagePlugin","signature":null},{"path":"PIL._binary","kind":"module","dispname":"_binary","docUri":"https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/internal_modules.html#module-PIL._binary","signature":null,"doc":"Binary input/output support routines.","doc_summary":"Binary input/output support routines."},{"path":"PIL._deprecate","kind":"module","dispname":"_deprecate","docUri":"https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/internal_modules.html#module-PIL._deprecate","signature":null},{"path":"PIL._imaging","kind":"module","dispname":"_imaging","docUri":"https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/internal_modules.html#module-PIL._imaging","signature":null},{"path":"PIL._tkinter_finder","kind":"module","dispname":"_tkinter_finder","docUri":"https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/internal_modules.html#module-PIL._tkinter_finder","signature":null,"doc":"Find compiled module linking to Tcl / Tk libraries","doc_summary":"Find compiled module linking to Tcl / Tk libraries"},{"path":"PIL._typing","kind":"module","dispname":"_typing","docUri":"https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/internal_modules.html#module-PIL._typing","signature":null},{"path":"PIL._util","kind":"module","dispname":"_util","docUri":"https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/internal_modules.html#module-PIL._util","signature":null},{"path":"PIL._version","kind":"module","dispname":"_version","docUri":"https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/internal_modules.html#module-PIL._version","signature":null},{"path":"PIL.features","kind":"package","dispname":"features","docUri":"https://pillow.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/features.html#module-PIL.features","signature":null},{"path":"PIL.__builtins__","kind":"variable","dispname":"__builtins__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"PIL.__cached__","kind":"constant","dispname":"__cached__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"PIL.__doc__","kind":"constant","dispname":"__doc__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"PIL.__file__","kind":"constant","dispname":"__file__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"PIL.__loader__","kind":"variable","dispname":"__loader__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"PIL.__name__","kind":"constant","dispname":"__name__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"PIL.__package__","kind":"constant","dispname":"__package__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"PIL.__path__","kind":"variable","dispname":"__path__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"PIL.__spec__","kind":"variable","dispname":"__spec__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"PIL.__version__","kind":"constant","dispname":"__version__","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"PIL._plugins","kind":"variable","dispname":"_plugins","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"PIL.BlpImagePlugin","kind":"package","dispname":"BlpImagePlugin","docUri":null,"signature":null,"doc":"Blizzard Mipmap Format (.blp)\nJerome Leclanche <jerome@leclan.ch>\n\nThe contents of this file are hereby released in the public domain (CC0)\nFull text of the CC0 license:\n  https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\n\nBLP1 files, used mostly in Warcraft III, are not fully supported.\nAll types of BLP2 files used in World of Warcraft are supported.\n\nThe BLP file structure consists of a header, up to 16 mipmaps of the\ntexture\n\nTexture sizes must be powers of two, though the two dimensions do\nnot have to be equal; 512x256 is valid, but 512x200 is not.\nThe first mipmap (mipmap #0) is the full size image; each subsequent\nmipmap halves both dimensions. The final mipmap should be 1x1.\n\nBLP files come in many different flavours:\n* JPEG-compressed (type == 0) - only supported for BLP1.\n* RAW images (type == 1, encoding == 1). Each mipmap is stored as an\n  array of 8-bit values, one per pixel, left to right, top to bottom.\n  Each value is an index to the palette.\n* DXT-compressed (type == 1, encoding == 2):\n- DXT1 compression is used if alpha_encoding == 0.\n  - An additional alpha bit is used if alpha_depth == 1.\n  - DXT3 compression is used if alpha_encoding == 1.\n  - DXT5 compression is used if alpha_encoding == 7.","doc_summary":"Blizzard Mipmap Format (.blp) Jerome Leclanche <jerome@leclan.ch>"},{"path":"PIL.FtexImagePlugin","kind":"package","dispname":"FtexImagePlugin","docUri":null,"signature":null,"doc":"A Pillow loader for .ftc and .ftu files (FTEX)\nJerome Leclanche <jerome@leclan.ch>\n\nThe contents of this file are hereby released in the public domain (CC0)\nFull text of the CC0 license:\n  https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\n\nIndependence War 2: Edge Of Chaos - Texture File Format - 16 October 2001\n\nThe textures used for 3D objects in Independence War 2: Edge Of Chaos are in a\npacked custom format called FTEX. This file format uses file extensions FTC\nand FTU.\n* FTC files are compressed textures (using standard texture compression).\n* FTU files are not compressed.\nTexture File Format\nThe FTC and FTU texture files both use the same format. This\nhas the following structure:\n{header}\n{format_directory}\n{data}\nWhere:\n{header} = {\n    u32:magic,\n    u32:version,\n    u32:width,\n    u32:height,\n    u32:mipmap_count,\n    u32:format_count\n}\n\n* The \"magic\" number is \"FTEX\".\n* \"width\" and \"height\" are the dimensions of the texture.\n* \"mipmap_count\" is the number of mipmaps in the texture.\n* \"format_count\" is the number of texture formats (different versions of the\nsame texture) in this file.\n\n{format_directory} = format_count * { u32:format, u32:where }\n\nThe format value is 0 for DXT1 compressed textures and 1 for 24-bit RGB\nuncompressed textures.\nThe texture data for a format starts at the position \"where\" in the file.\n\nEach set of texture data in the file has the following structure:\n{data} = format_count * { u32:mipmap_size, mipmap_size * { u8 } }\n* \"mipmap_size\" is the number of bytes in that mip level. For compressed\ntextures this is the size of the texture data compressed with DXT1. For 24 bit\nuncompressed textures, this is 3 * width * height. Following this are the image\nbytes for that mipmap level.\n\nNote: All data is stored in little-Endian (Intel) byte order.","doc_summary":"A Pillow loader for .ftc and .ftu files (FTEX) Jerome Leclanche <jerome@leclan.ch>"},{"path":"PIL.PdfParser","kind":"package","dispname":"PdfParser","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"PIL.QoiImagePlugin","kind":"package","dispname":"QoiImagePlugin","docUri":null,"signature":null},{"path":"PIL.report","kind":"module","dispname":"report","docUri":null,"signature":null}]}
